  "steps": [
    "Marinate seitan with soy sauce, sugar, and water for 10–15 minutes.",
    "Whisk all sauce ingredients together until sugar dissolves. Set aside.",
    "Heat 1 tbsp oil in a wok over medium-high heat. Sear seitan in a single layer 1–2 minutes per side until lightly browned. Remove and set aside.",
    "Add remaining oil. Add garlic and chilli flakes and cook 10–15 seconds until fragrant (do not burn).",
    "Add sliced onion and cook 1 minute. Add carrot and broccoli and stir fry 1–2 minutes. Add pak choi stems, cook 30 seconds, then add leaves and cook until just wilted.",
    "Add rice noodles and pour sauce over. Toss gently and let noodles sit undisturbed 20–30 seconds to develop slight char.",
    "Return seitan to the pan. Add basil and toss briefly until wilted. Serve immediately."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "High heat is key for smoky flavour and proper charring.",
    "Do not overcook seitan or it will become chewy.",
    "If too salty, add a small splash of water; if flat, add a squeeze of lime.",
    "Let noodles sit briefly in the pan to develop caramelised edges."
  ]
